# qumo relay — environment variable configuration example
#
# Usage:
#   export $(grep -v '^#' relay.env | xargs)   # bash/zsh
#   qumo relay
#
# For systemd deployments, use:
#   EnvironmentFile=/etc/qumo/relay.env
#
# For Docker:
#   docker run --env-file relay.env ghcr.io/qumo-dev/qumo relay

# ─── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Address to bind the relay server (QUIC/MoQT).
RELAY_ADDR=0.0.0.0:4433

# TLS certificate and key.
# Set INSECURE=true to generate an ephemeral self-signed cert (dev/test only).
CERT_FILE=certs/server.crt
KEY_FILE=certs/server.key
# INSECURE=true

# ─── mTLS (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PEM CA certificate. When set, mutual TLS is enabled:
#   - incoming peer connections that present a cert are verified against this CA;
#   - the dialer presents this node's CERT_FILE cert to remote relays and
#     trusts only the CA pool;
#   - remote resolver clients also present the client cert and verify the
#     remote server against this CA (when REMOTE_TLS_ENABLED=true).
# Connections WITHOUT a client cert are still allowed by default (browser-compatible).
# Leave unset to disable mTLS entirely (default).
# CA_FILE=certs/ca.crt

# When true, every connection MUST present a client cert signed by CA_FILE.
# Use this for relay-only clusters with no direct browser traffic.
# Default: false (cert is verified if presented, missing cert is allowed).
# MTLS_REQUIRED=true

# ─── Node identity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Human-readable node identifier (defaults to hostname).
RELAY_NAME=relay-tokyo

# Geographic region label (arbitrary string, e.g. "asia", "europe").
REGION=asia

# Node role: "hub" (inter-region) or "edge" (client-facing).
# Leave empty for a standalone relay.
ROLE=hub

# Public address advertised to peers.
# Required when RELAY_ADDR is a wildcard (0.0.0.0 / ::).
ADVERTISE_ADDR=relay-tokyo.example.com:4433

# ─── Capacity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Maximum number of group caches held in memory (default: 100).
# GROUP_CACHE_SIZE=100

# Frame buffer size in bytes (default: 1500, roughly one network MTU).
# FRAME_CAPACITY=1500

# ─── Static peers (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Comma-separated list of peer relay addresses.
# The node connects to each peer and relays their announcements.
# PEERS=moqt://relay-london.example.com:4433,moqt://relay-newyork.example.com:4433

# ─── Local resolver — Nomad-native discovery (optional) ─────────────────────

# Nomad HTTP API address (set automatically when running inside Nomad).
# Default: http://localhost:4646
# LOCAL_RESOLVER_ADDR=http://localhost:4646

# Nomad service name to query for peer discovery (default: "qumo-relay").
# The service must be defined in Nomad job specs with tags for role and region.
# Hub nodes should be tagged with "hub", edge nodes with "edge".
# Region tags can be "region=us-east", "region=asia", etc.
# LOCAL_RESOLVER_SERVICE_NAME=qumo-relay

# Polling interval for local service discovery (default: 15s).
# LOCAL_RESOLVER_INTERVAL=15s

# ─── Enterprise (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the qumo-enterprise server. When set, the relay:
#   - authenticates publisher JWTs via POST /v1/credentials/introspect;
#   - reports cumulative ingress/egress byte totals via POST /v1/usage/events.
# Leave unset to disable enterprise features (open relay mode).
# QUMO_ENTERPRISE_URL=https://enterprise.example.com

# Shared bearer token that the relay presents to qumo-enterprise.
# Must match the QUMO_RELAY_TOKEN configured on the enterprise server.
# QUMO_RELAY_TOKEN=supersecret

# ─── Remote traffic resolver (optional) ────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the remote traffic resolver (e.g. qumo-enterprise control plane).
# When set, cross-cluster hub discovery is enabled via this endpoint.
# REMOTE_RESOLVER_URL=https://traffic-resolver.example.com:8443

# Optional bearer token sent to the remote resolver for authentication.
# REMOTE_AUTH_TOKEN=supersecret

# Polling interval for remote resolver (default: 15s).
# REMOTE_RESOLVE_INTERVAL=15s

# Enable TLS for the remote resolver connection (default: false).
# When true, mTLS uses the relay's CERT_FILE and CA_FILE for client auth.
# REMOTE_TLS_ENABLED=true
